 ],
 "text": "What if the Internet went down tomorrow, for 30 days? Hour 1. Your card stops working at the coffee shop. Only 14 and 100 payments in the US are still made in cash, according to the Federal Reserve. Day 1. More than 99 and 100 bits of data between continents travel through cables on the seafloor, with the network down, banks, airlines, and hospitals fall back to paper. Day 3. Stores reordered by phone and shelves start to thin out. Week 2. Neighbors trade favors, and the radio becomes the news again. Day 30. The Internet comes back on, and nobody remembers their passwords. Would you last 30 days offline? Follow for part 2."
